## Facts (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/d-cpp-package-lz4-summary.md` BLOCKERS)
`stream_connector_consumer.cmake:30` runs the install with `--config Release` regardless of the
producer's configuration. On this Debug single-config (Ninja) tree the install copies
`zlink_stream_connector_cppTargets.cmake` but not `zlink_stream_connector_cppTargets-debug.cmake`
(the per-config file for the built Debug locations), so the consumer configure fails at
`stream_connector_consumer.cmake:97`: `IMPORTED_LOCATION not set for imported target
"zlink::stream_connector"`. `install_consumer.cmake` (the Framework package test) passes on the same
tree — compare how it selects the configuration and mirror it.

## What to do
Make the stream-connector package test pass the producer's actual configuration (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE
for single-config generators, `$<CONFIG>`/CTest -C for multi-config) to both the install step and the
consumer build, keeping vcpkg/Release behaviour unchanged. Verify
`ctest --test-dir build/linux-ninja-c-e2e -R '^test_cpp_stream_connector_install_consumer$' --output-on-failure`
3× and `test_cpp_framework_install_consumer` 1×.

